+// F2 FORK A (2026-09-25): high-water pricing for overwrite/kill verification.
+// A free WEAKEN (or any downward redeclare) must not discount the erase price:
+// the lawful effort for erasing a judgment is n(HW), where HW is the maximum
+// strength the judgment ever held during its lifetime. The lifetime starts at
+// the most recent OK ADD or OVERWRITE before the checked op (a fresh judgment
+// resets the water mark); every OK strength-write (ADD/STRENGTHEN/WEAKEN/
+// TRAINER_DECLARE/OVERWRITE) in [birth, idx) contributes its after-strength
+// (word 14 & 255). On trails with no downward redeclare, HW == before-strength
+// and behavior is unchanged.
+fn ck_birth_idx(s:*StStore,slot:i32,upto:i32)i32 {
+    let i:i32=upto-1;
+    while(i>=0){
